# default.pipx -- declarative list of Python applications installed via pipx.
#
# This is the HOST-SIDE bucket for Python-only pentest tools (Phase 3). pipx
# installs each app into its own isolated venv under ~/.local with a shim on
# ~/.local/bin (already on PATH in Bluefin), so installs live in the user's
# writable layer -- NOT baked into the image, NOT run at boot. Same no-layering
# posture as brew, and Track-B-friendly (pipx + python3 exist on the GNOME OS
# bootc base too).
#
# WHEN A TOOL BELONGS HERE (vs. the Kali container):
#   * It is a Python CLI app with no clean homebrew-core formula, AND
#   * it installs WITHOUT system build dependencies -- i.e. it ships a pure
#     `py3-none-any` wheel or otherwise needs no apt/dnf -devel headers.
# A Python tool that needs build headers (e.g. anything pulling `gssapi`, which
# needs libkrb5-dev/krb5-devel) can NOT be installed host-side under the
# no-layering policy -- it goes in the Kali container (apt-installable there).
#
# FORMAT: one `pipx install` spec per line -- a PyPI name, `name==version`, or
# a `git+https://...` URL. Comments must be on their OWN line (a leading `#`);
# do not put `#` comments after a spec, because git URLs may contain a
# `#egg=`/`#subdirectory=` fragment. Installed by: ujust install-pipx-tools

# AD privesc swiss-army-knife (CravateRouge/bloodyAD). Pure-Python wheel
# (py3-none-any), no system build deps -> clean host install.
bloodyAD

# BloodHound ingestor that collects over ADWS/SOAP (the Python soaphound, NOT
# the .NET FalconForce tool of the same name). Ships a py3-none-any wheel with
# a `soaphound` console entry point. Its one real dependency is impacket, which
# is pure-Python and whose only compiled transitive deps (cryptography via
# pyOpenSSL, pycryptodomex) install from prebuilt manylinux wheels -- so NO
# system build headers are needed. Crucially impacket does NOT pull gssapi, so
# the libkrb5-dev problem that routed powerview.py to the container (below)
# does not apply here. Verified against the sdist/PyPI 2026-06.
soaphound

# BloodHound's Active Directory ingestor for BHCE (NOT legacy bloodhound-python
# -- only compatible with BloodHound CE). The CLI is `bloodhound-ce-python`;
# the PyPI package is `bloodhound-ce`, which provides that entry point. Same
# author/lineage as impacket, same shape as soaphound above: a py3-none-any
# wheel whose deps (dnspython, impacket, ldap3, pyasn1, pycryptodome) are all
# pure-Python or ship prebuilt manylinux wheels -- no gssapi, no build headers.
# Verified against the sdist/PyPI 2026-06.
bloodhound-ce

# Web Application Firewall fingerprinting toolkit. Pure-Python (py3-none-any),
# deps are requests/requests[socks] only -> clean host install. Not in
# homebrew-core, hence pipx rather than brew.
wafw00f

# HTTP parameter discovery suite. Pure-Python; deps requests/dicttoxml/ratelimit,
# no build headers. Has a brew formula but with NO Linux bottle, so per the
# host-side rubric it lands here (pipx) instead of brew.
arjun

# AD Certificate Services enumeration and exploitation toolkit (ly4k/Certipy).
# Covers the full ESC1-ESC16 attack path family against AD CS. Pure Python
# (py3-none-any wheel, verified against PyPI 2026-06). Deps are impacket,
# ldap3, pyasn1, pycryptodome, cryptography -- all ship prebuilt manylinux
# wheels, no system build headers required. Named `certipy-ad` on PyPI
# (the older `certipy` package is a different, unrelated tool).
certipy-ad

# TLS/SSL analysis tool (nabla-c0d3/sslyze). Connects to servers and checks
# ciphers, protocols, certificates, and known TLS vulns (Heartbleed, ROBOT,
# CCS injection, CRIME, etc.). Uses nassl (a C OpenSSL wrapper), but nassl
# ships prebuilt manylinux2014_x86_64 wheels for Python 3.10+ -- no build
# headers needed on Bluefin / Fedora host. Distinct from the host-brew
# `sslscan` (which does cipher enumeration only): sslyze does deeper protocol
# analysis and structured JSON output useful for automated scanning pipelines.
sslyze

# Active Directory LDAP dumper (dirkjanm/ldapdomaindump). Enumerates users,
# groups, computers, policies, and trusts from AD via LDAP and writes
# HTML/JSON/grep-friendly output. Pure Python (deps: ldap3, dnspython, future
# -- all py3-none-any or manylinux wheels, no build headers). Complements
# BloodHound CE ingestors: ldapdomaindump gives quick human-readable output
# without standing up Neo4j, useful for fast first-look at an AD environment.
ldapdomaindump

# --- Deliberately NOT host-side (documented per-tool decisions) -------------
# powerview.py: needs the gssapi C extension, which requires libkrb5-dev
#   headers at build time. gssapi ships no Linux manylinux wheels and always
#   builds from source -- so host-side brew pipx cannot install it (no headers,
#   no-layering policy). Routed to the Kali container instead, where libkrb5-dev
#   and python3-pipx are baked into additional_packages for exactly this purpose.
#   Install it with: ujust setup-powerview
#
# wfuzz: only a stale Python-2 third-party brew tap exists and upstream is
#   effectively abandoned on modern Python -- not pipx-installable host-side.
#   Now baked directly into the container's additional_packages (apt) instead;
#   see custom/distrobox/spinofin-kali.ini.
